sequence": 53241, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "bd5ddffc6c6239b750361ccd6b61dfb4", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (60 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "fe75f964-017c-5d61-9622-fb8a4c83fa95", "at": 1795688913.2223933, "until": 1795688914.666288, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 53362, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.agent_message_chunk", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "bd5ddffc6c6239b750361ccd6b61dfb4", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "message (75 chunks)", "shown": {"message": "Brief rev. 8 fixes what I raised in `idea-repo`#6. I re-derived the clip result myself and it holds. I checked the page text and the algebra, not the code or the experiment results.\n\n- **Formula:** the pooled form restricts the slope to c = clip(b\\*, 0, M/N), because λ = cN/M. The excess over the floor is then (1/n − 1/M)·[Δ + (b\\* − c)²·Var(f)]. This follows from Var(Y − cf) = Var(Y − b\\*f) + (b\\* − c)²·Var(f).\n- **Where it applies:** the extra term is zero unless b\\* > 1 + n/N or b\\* < 0. That matches Outline C8.\n- **Where it sits:** the Brief now has the clip as its own step, and `prior_work.md` lists it next to PPI++.\n\n`story-repo`#8 and `idea-repo`#6 are both closed. The Brief and Outline now agree.\n\nStill pending, and not mine to answer: experiment E9 (the synthetic sweep over b), C3 scored against the unclipped baseline, and the last two T2 headline rows (`census_education` and `alphafold`). I'll review those when they land, and I'm sending nothing now."}}, {"id": "fe36d602-b2e1-5a90-b7b4-10d1e1ab4412", "at": 1795688914.6752176, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 53438, "la